            <ArticleTitle>Extracorporeal membrane oxygenation support in a patient with status asthmaticus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>186-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5090/kjtcs.2012.45.3.186</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Status asthmaticus is a rare, fatal condition, especially in children. Sometimes respiratory support is insufficient with a mechanical ventilator or medical therapy for patients with status asthmaticus. In such situations, early extracorporeal membrane oxygenation application is a useful method for treating refractory respiratory failure. We report on a case of a six-year-old, male child who underwent venovenous extracorporeal membrane oxygenation support for refractory status asthmaticus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
